@startuml session_directory_continuation
skinparam BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam maxMessageSize 72
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0D47A1
    LifeLineBorderColor #1565C0
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantBorderColor #1565C0
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantFontColor #000000
}
hide footbox

title Session Continuation — Select, Plan, Materialize, and Launch

actor Operator
participant "Session Browser TUI" as TUI
participant "Directory / Lineage" as Directory
participant "Continuation Planner" as Planner
participant "Source Node" as Source
participant "Target Node" as Target
participant "AX Data Plane" as AX
participant "Session Cloning" as Clone
participant "Target Terminal" as Terminal
participant "macOS Aqua Broker" as Broker

autonumber

== Selection and pure planning ==

Operator -> TUI: select lineage/session instance
TUI -> Directory: resolve exact entry and current catalog head
Directory --> TUI: instances, owner, freshness, annotations, warnings
Operator -> TUI: choose intent, target host, target environment
TUI -> Planner: plan continuation from observed head
Planner -> Source: revalidate instance, source head, runtime, lease
Source --> Planner: authoritative source facts or mismatch
Planner -> Target: probe environment tuple, auth availability, workspace
Target --> Planner: capabilities and destination facts
Planner -> Planner: select route and build content-addressed plan
Planner --> TUI: steps, fidelity, bytes, risks, expiry, confirmations

alt Plan unavailable or policy rejected
    break Refused plan terminates without execution
        TUI --> Operator: explain blocker; no mutation
    end
else Exactly one safe non-mutating attach/resume route
    TUI -> Planner: execute unique non-mutating route
else Operator confirms exact plan
    Operator -> TUI: execute PLAN_ID
    TUI -> Planner: execute with expected source/target facts
end

== Revalidation and execution ==

Planner -> Source: verify head/lease/runtime still match
Planner -> Target: verify tuple/workspace/auth still match

alt Remote attach to current owner
    Planner -> AX: authenticate attach to current winning owner
    AX --> Planner: existing owner endpoint; no lease/runtime mutation
    break Remote attach terminates without target finalization
        Planner --> TUI: authenticated current-owner attach command
        TUI -> Terminal: remote attach to existing owner terminal
        Terminal --> Operator: interactive native agent terminal
    end
else Same managed owner and environment
    Planner -> AX: revalidate existing winning lease and execution realm
    opt Current-owner resume target is macOS
        AX -> Broker: attest existing broker/server + provider auth
        Broker --> AX: generation/build/macOS-bound evidence
    end
    AX -> Terminal: create/resume under existing winning lease
    break Current-owner resume terminates without ownership finalization
        Terminal --> Planner: current-owner runtime/attach evidence
        Planner --> TUI: resumed current-owner identity and attach command
        TUI -> Terminal: local attach to current-owner runtime
        Terminal --> Operator: interactive native agent terminal
    end
else Ownership takeover without conversion
    Planner -> AX: checkpoint, transfer, materialize, lease handoff
else Fork or same-environment clone
    Planner -> AX: fork/materialize new managed session
else Cross-environment continuation
    Planner -> Clone: capture, canonicalize, project, validate target
    Clone -> AX: transfer artifacts and publish lineage
end

opt Ownership-creating target is macOS
    Target -> Broker: prove broker + separate provider-auth readiness
    Broker --> Target: generation/build/macOS-bound evidence
end
AX -> Target: finalize managed target and winning ownership
Target -> Terminal: create runtime after ownership commit
Terminal --> Target: runtime/attach evidence
Target --> Planner: committed target and attach plan
Planner --> TUI: target identity, fidelity, lineage, attach command
TUI -> Terminal: local attach to created target runtime
Terminal --> Operator: interactive native agent terminal

@enduml
